          ],
          "benefits_md": "\n- Enables farmers to sell their produce at government-approved procurement centers.\n\n\n- Ensures fair pricing through the Minimum Support Price (MSP) announced by the government.\n- Provides a transparent and digital platform for registration and sale.\n- Payment for the procured crop is made directly to the farmer’s bank account through online transfer.\n\n<br>\n\n",
          "briefDescription": "The scheme aims to ensure fair crop prices for farmers by facilitating government procurement and provides easy online registration for landholding farmers to sell their crops at minimum support price. ",
          "detailedDescription": [
            {
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "The “Registration for Crop Procurement” scheme was launched by the Department of Food, Civil Supplies, and Consumer Protection, Government of Madhya Pradesh. The scheme aims to ensure that farmers in the state receive a fair and remunerative price for their crops by facilitating government procurement, allowing landholding farmers to register for selling their produce at government-designated procurement centers at the Minimum Support Price (MSP). A plan has been made to cover the entire Madhya Pradesh through the e-Uparjan Application, through which the grains (wheat, paddy, sorghum, millet, gram, lentils, mustard, etc.) of all the districts of the state are monitored."
                }
              ],
              "type": "paragraph"
            },
